A: The Sys Json class will handle the conversion for you. The object Sys holds your input and stores it from user. Your products data can be stored in object Product. All the fields(id, name, other details) can be stored in it. Finally the converted data could be output in json format. I hope that will help!

A: You can try the following logic. You just have to add more products for which you want recommendations.
$products = ['{id: 1, name:'Electric toothbrush', product: 0, }','{id: 2, name:'Electric toothbrush', product: 0, }'];
      $names = array();
      foreach($products as $prod){
        $names[] = $prod['name'];
      }

      $names = array_unique($names);
      $results = [];
      foreach($names as $name){
        foreach($products as $prod){
          if($prod['name']==$name){
            if(isset($results[$name])){
              $results[$name]++;
            }
            else{
              $results[$name] = 1;
            }
         }
        }
      }

      echo json_encode($results);

Let me know if this works for your situation.
